-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Dynamite Dan
  Publisher   Mirrorsoft, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dynamite Dan (1985)(Mirrorsoft).z80
  MD5         3470d12b21edb24d6b665dfac5e8d84d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.09% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe
              0xC80A (the main loop, once a tick); input keyed to ticks;
              lockstep on lives and room; 10 trials per scene of up to 300
              ticks (the mean; single trials -0.6 to +0.5 percent))

  Changes     1.0: Dan as Next sprites, the airship's hull and cables in front
              of him; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM, so the game
              starts from its own BASIC; the game's speed restored after every
              hook; R kept as the original's

  Note        Keys: a key on the loading screen, then ENTER on the menu. In
              play A left, S right, SPACE jump, P pause. Dan is a Next sprite
              in bright cyan over his own pixels, the look the owner approved,
              and in the airship room the hull and cables are drawn in front
              of him, so he stands inside the basket; the rooms, enemies and
              panel keep the original's colours. The hook costs about 0.1
              percent of the game's pace (never faster); the game has no
              padding to repay it from. It starts from the tape's own BASIC.
              Cheats from the archive's POKEs for this release (two names
              shortened for the menu: Energy bar never decreases, Disable "Q
              Quit" key); dropped: Manipulate teleports, Water can't kill you,
              Picked up oxygen bottle and Speed up game (their code was never
              reached in the simulator's play, so not shown to work), Dynamite
              sticks found (asks for a value). Dan's sprite moves as his plot
              starts, so once in a few hundred frames it is a frame ahead of
              the game's own pixels under it. Not tested on hardware.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  No enemies
   3  Energy never decreases
   4  Disable Q quit key

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

