-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 52 recordings, 122,380 frames: 22,117 Dan plots,
              269 screen clears (the ending's hide in unit cases only): at
              every hook original and patched code compared from the same
              state, every register with R, memory, Dan's sprite pixels
              against the original plotter's ink, the airship's hull and
              cables against the live screen in room 43; 27 negative controls
              detected on the states of each recording, a forced 3.5 MHz exit
              (entered at 7 MHz) and R one off among them; ROM path check
              clean on both builds, the BASIC start included

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: the snapshot's own BASIC start, the menu
              and play reached from the .nxc's menu build, cheats on and off,
              frames inspected; flicker check over 300 frames: 1 frame with
              Dan's sprite a frame ahead of his own ULA pixels (the same cyan)
              and 1 one-frame attribute change, the latter also in the
              approved build; 15-minute soak: no freeze, loop or crash

  Coverage    Random-play recordings only, no human play: one from the TOSEC
              file's BASIC start (rooms 0, 43, 44), 48 room-census starts,
              deaths, water, the airship room; not reached: the ending (all 8
              dynamite sticks and the airship), the lifts measured

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
